        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Anatomy of an Active Black Hole</title>\n<style>\n    body {\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 0;\n        background-color: #222;\n        font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n        color: white;\n    }\n    .container {\n        max-width: 800px;\n        margin: 0 auto;\n        background-color: #000;\n    }\n    .placeholder {\n        background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n        border: 1px dashed rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);\n        display: flex;\n        align-items: center;\n        justify-content: center;\n        text-align: center;\n        color: #aaa;\n        font-size: 12px;\n        box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n    h2 {\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 20px 20px 10px 20px;\n        font-size: 26px;\n        font-weight: bold;\n    }\n    p {\n        margin: 0 0 10px 0;\n        line-height: 1.4;\n        font-size: 14px;\n    }\n    \n    /* Header */\n    .header {\n        display: flex;\n        align-items: center;\n        padding: 15px 20px;\n        background-color: #000;\n    }\n    .header .logo {\n        width: 60px;\n        height: 50px;\n        margin-right: 15px;\n        border-radius: 50%;\n    }\n    .header .text {\n        font-size: 12px;\n        line-height: 1.3;\n    }\n\n    /* Section 1 */\n    .sec1 {\n        background-color: #2d1138;\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\n    }\n    .sec1-images {\n        position: relative;\n        height: 380px;\n        margin: 0 20px;\n    }\n    .sec1-img1 {\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 20px;\n        left: 0;\n        width: 260px;\n        height: 260px;\n        border-radius: 50%;\n    }\n    .sec1-text1 {\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 50px;\n        left: 0;\n        width: 260px;\n        text-align: center;\n        font-size: 13px;\n        text-shadow: 1px 1px 3px black;\n    }\n    .sec1-img2 {\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 80px;\n        left: 230px;\n        width: 300px;\n        height: 300px;\n        border-radius: 50%;\n        z-index: 2;\n    }\n    .sec1-text2 {\n        position: absolute;\n        bottom: 40px;\n        left: 230px;\n        width: 300px;\n        text-align: center;\n        font-size: 13px;\n        text-shadow: 1px 1px 3px black;\n        z-index: 3;\n    }\n    .sec1-img3 {\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 0;\n        right: 0;\n        width: 240px;\n        height: 240px;\n        border-radius: 50%;\n    }\n    .sec1-text3 {\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 40px;\n        right: 0;\n        width: 240px;\n        text-align: center;\n        font-size: 13px;\n        text-shadow: 1px 1px 3px black;\n    }\n    .sec1-bottom {\n        display: flex;\n        justify-content: space-between;\n        padding: 0 20px;\n        margin-top: 20px;\n    }\n    .sec1-bottom p {\n        width: 45%;\n        font-size: 13px;\n    }\n    .sec1-bottom p:last-child {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n\n    /* Section 2 */\n    .sec2 {\n        background-color: #3d2612;\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\n    }\n    .sec2-content {\n        display: flex;\n        justify-content: space-between;\n        align-items: center;\n        padding: 10px 20px;\n    }\n    .sec2-img {\n        width: 260px;\n        height: 260px;\n        border-radius: 50%;\n    }\n    .sec2-text-mid {\n        width: 220px;\n        text-align: center;\n        font-size: 14px;\n    }\n    .sec2-text-mid p {\n        margin-bottom: 20px;\n    }\n    .sec2-text-mid i {\n        font-style: italic;\n        font-weight: bold;\n    }\n    .sec2-bottom {\n        display: flex;\n        justify-content: space-between;\n        padding: 0 30px;\n        margin-top: 10px;\n    }\n    .sec2-bottom p {\n        width: 42%;\n        font-size: 13px;\n        text-align: center;\n    }\n\n    /* Section 3 */\n    .sec3 {\n        background-color: #121f3d;\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\n        position: relative;\n    }\n    .sec3-bg {\n        width: 100%;\n        height: 350px;\n        border: none;\n    }\n    .sec3-text {\n        position: absolute;\n        top: 50%;\n        left: 50%;\n        transform: translate(-50%, -50%);\n        text-align: center;\n        width: 80%;\n        text-shadow: 1px 1px 4px black;\n    }\n    .sec3-text p {\n        font-size: 15px;\n        margin-bottom: 20px;\n    }\n    .sec3-text i {\n        font-style: italic;\n        font-weight: bold;\n    }\n\n    /* Section 4 */\n    .sec4 {\n        background-color: #0f3d26;\n        padding-bottom: 20px;\n    }\n    .sec4-content {\n        display: flex;\n        padding: 10px 20px;\n        gap: 20px;\n    }\n    .sec4-left {\n        width: 32%;\n    }\n    .sec4-left-img {\n        width: 100%;\n        height: 160px;\n        margin-bottom: 15px;\n    }\n    .sec4-left p {\n        font-size: 13px;\n        margin-bottom: 15px;\n    }\n    .sec4-left i {\n        font-style: italic;\n        font-weight: bold;\n    }\n    .sec4-right {\n        width: 68%;\n    }\n    .sec4-right-img {\n        width: 100%;\n        height: 380px;\n        margin-bottom: 10px;\n    }\n    .sec4-right p {\n        font-size: 13px;\n    }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"container\">\n    <!-- Header -->\n    <div class=\"header\">\n        <div class=\"placeholder logo\">[NASA Logo]</div>\n        <div class=\"text\">\n            Jet Propulsion Laboratory<br>\n            California Institute of Technology\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Section 1 -->\n    <div class=\"sec1\">\n        <h2>Anatomy of an Active Black Hole</h2>\n        <div class=\"sec1-images\">\n            <div class=\"placeholder sec1-img1\">[Image: Supermassive Black Hole]</div>\n            <div class=\"sec1-text1\">\n                Supermassive Black Hole<br>\n                <i>Size: as big as Mercury's orbit</i>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"placeholder sec1-img2\">[Image: \"Doughnut\" Ring of Dust & Gas]</div>\n            <div class=\"sec1-text2\">\n                \"Doughnut\" Ring of Dust & Gas<br>\n                <i>Size: around 1 light-year</i>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"placeholder sec1-img3\">[Image: Host Galaxy]</div>\n            <div class=\"sec1-text3\">\n                Host Galaxy<br>\n                <i>Size: about 100,000 light-years</i>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"sec1-bottom\">\n            <p>Astronomers call supermassive black<br>holes and their surrounding disks<br>\"Active Galactic Nuclei\" or \"AGN\"</p>\n            <p>Black holes emit no light, but<br>the glow from the bright<br>material swirling around them<br>can be seen by telescopes.</p>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Section 2 -->\n    <div class=\"sec2\">\n        <h2>Why Do Active Black Holes Look Different?</h2>\n        <div class=\"sec2-content\">\n            <div class=\"placeholder sec2-img\">[Image: Face-on view of black hole]</div>\n            <div class=\"sec2-text-mid\">\n                <p>In some galaxies the<br>black hole regions are<br><i>incredibly bright</i>, while in<br>other galaxies they<br>appear <i>much darker</i>.</p>\n                <p>A \"unified model\"<br>suggests the angle at<br>which we view them can<br>explain the differences.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"placeholder sec2-img\">[Image: Edge-on view of black hole]</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"sec2-bottom\">\n            <p>Seen face-on, we detect the light from the<br>hot material surrounding the black hole.</p>\n            <p>When viewed through the edge of the dusty<br>doughnut, the black hole is hidden.</p>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Section 3 -->\n    <div class=\"sec3\">\n        <h2>What We Expect to See</h2>\n        <div class=\"placeholder sec3-bg\">[Image: Scattered galaxies in various orientations]</div>\n        <div class=\"sec3-text\">\n            <p>Galaxies are oriented randomly in the sky so the disks<br>in their centers should be oriented randomly as well.</p>\n            <p>Thus we expect to see a random mix of exposed and<br>hidden black holes <i>everywhere we look</i>.</p>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- Section 4 -->\n    <div class=\"sec4\">\n        <h2>WISE Observations Challenge \"Unified Model\"</h2>\n        <div class=\"sec4-content\">\n            <div class=\"sec4-left\">\n                <div class=\"placeholder sec4-left-img\">[Image: WISE Satellite]</div>\n                <p>Observations with NASA's Wide-<br>field Infrared Survey Explorer<br>reveal that hidden black holes<br>tend to be <i>more clumped<br>together</i> than exposed ones.</p>\n                <p>This violates the \"unified model,\"<br>which predicts we should see<br>the same random distribution of<br>dusty doughnuts regardless of<br>how clumped the objects are.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"sec4-right\">\n                <div class=\"placeholder sec4-right-img\">[Image: Strongly clumped galaxies shown in purple]</div>\n                <p>Strongly clumped galaxies are likely to have larger halos of dark matter (shown<br>artistically here in purple), which might provide a clue about what else besides the<br>doughnuts could be hiding the black holes.</p>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>"
